orname{sin}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365665} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ad3991-2ac6-5ad3-a913-929c3b64178c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac97a07e-cd49-5c84-a334-f6d1792e26ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac97a07e-cd49-5c84-a334-f6d1792e26ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365667} :answer-field/id #uuid "918694ef-b209-599f-9859-2c7968e720c9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "511649c4-cd9c-5496-8df1-bb8892a20547" :question/math-academy-id "q-334386" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & -6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=6\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-6\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((6\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(6\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(6\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+6\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1666e2ac-b3fe-5abf-bf6c-480c904e35c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308916} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0e242e-f8bc-5b61-92f4-057c108c04c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309064} {:answer/id #uuid "39e9ae43-ec84-53c1-9ff5-1cab8a1513fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309193} {:answer/id #uuid "7270f518-034e-590f-9bf1-e3034ee21c3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309637} {:answer/id #uuid "88c4bae8-f281-5b85-b676-befbbaf6a7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7270f518-034e-590f-9bf1-e3034ee21c3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309637} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd0c097-ae2f-556e-9141-4922553f97a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d589487-f539-5a2a-9c68-978fcbd8d916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308974} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7f3a02-4a57-5a6f-82ac-295a09b04201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309351} {:answer/id #uuid "801400d7-5f92-5160-aa74-65afe20e1479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309754} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c6ca05-bdfb-57f3-acf6-42e584e9e189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d589487-f539-5a2a-9c68-978fcbd8d916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308974} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ac3f93-6295-5f30-bd13-d2e6c1a521c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213cd977-7f18-51d2-9f21-28d4b1a5fa0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308999} {:answer/id #uuid "5b75abdf-0c2f-5971-941e-b26da9a01df8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309435} {:answer/id #uuid "85a84435-5c8a-5585-b8e5-e8bffe321073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309787} {:answer/id #uuid "eac98a1a-0bc6-5585-badc-67bd9c21bfee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310617} {:answer/id #uuid "fe87b04f-2863-5764-85be-e1341c2b05ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "213cd977-7f18-51d2-9f21-28d4b1a5fa0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308999} :answer-field/id #uuid "b40a4c73-e790-56ac-96c9-d5fa994ccaf7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d9725c1-fcc5-57a9-8b5a-bd5efbda8207" :question/math-academy-id "q-336093" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states the independence of the columns of {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L3}$ by the {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L2}.$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states that the two columns of $Φ(t)$ are linearly independent, which is required of a fundamental matrix. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ states independence of the columns of $Φ(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Recall that a square matrix is invertible when its determinant is nonzero. Since in $\\text{L3}$ we have that $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t,$ it follows that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$ Thus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by the $\\text{properties of invertible matrices}.$"}]}
